<PageLayout title="Research">
  <section class="stack">
    <h1 class="h1 bl">Research</h1>
    <p class="lede">Two programs: one on the questions science has set aside, and one on how science goes about asking questions at all.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack">
    <h2 class="h2 bl">Fringe Science</h2>
    <p class="body">Many of the great discoveries began outside the consensus of their day. We believe science flourishes when unconventional ideas are allowed to compete openly and rigorously, and we support inquiry into areas that have been overlooked, constrained or dismissed too early.</p>
    <p class="sub">Theoretical physics, health and longevity, human cognition.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack">
    <h2 class="h2 bl">Scientific Epistemology</h2>
    <p class="body">How are research questions conceived, and how is laboratory work actually done? Science has long fixed on a single framework, the scientific method. This program looks for ways of thinking about research, and of working in the lab, that go beyond it.</p>
    <p class="sub">Metascience, philosophy of science, scientific methodology.</p>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
